---
title: Peruvian Green Sauce
description: Aji verde, a spicy, creamy green sauce of jalapeños, cilantro, and garlic blended with mayonnaise.
tags: [sauce]
course: condiment
icons: [pepper-hot, leafy-green, bottle-droplet]
cuisine: Peruvian
difficulty: easy
source:
  name: Skinnytaste
  author: Gina Homolka
  url: https://www.skinnytaste.com/peruvian-green-sauce/
yield: 1 2/3%cups
time: 10m
---

Cook the @red onion{1/4%cup}(chopped) in a #small skillet{} with @olive oil{1%tsp} until soft, ~cook{3-4%minutes}.

Move the onion to a #blender{}. Add the remaining @&olive oil{5%tsp}, @light mayonnaise{1/2%cup}, @white vinegar{2%tbsp}, @yellow mustard{4%tsp}, @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}, and @black pepper{1/4%tsp}(freshly ground).

Add the @jalapeños{3}(seeded but ribs left in, roughly chopped, about 1 cup or 3 oz), @fresh cilantro{57%g}(2 oz, about 2 cups chopped leaves and stems, rinsed well), and @garlic cloves{3}(medium, crushed through a press). Blend on high speed until the sauce is smooth and creamy, about ~blend{30%seconds}.

> **Storing** — Keeps in the refrigerator for at least a week. Halve the recipe if you won't use it all.
